{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":2180754,"ns":0,"title":"Donaldson's theorem","extract":"In mathematics, and especially differential topology and gauge theory, Donaldson's theorem states that a definite intersection form of a closed, oriented, smooth manifold of dimension 4 is diagonalizable. If the intersection form is positive (negative) definite, it can be diagonalized to the identity matrix (negative identity matrix) over the integers.","description":"On when a definite intersection form of a smooth 4-manifold is diagonalizable","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}